---
title: Onion Rings
servings: 4
course: Side
prep time: 10m
cook time: 15m
locale: en_GB
difficulty: Medium
cuisine: British
diet: Vegetarian
tags:
- vegetarian
- side-dish
- british
- savoury
---

Sift the @plain flour{100%g} into a bowl with @salt{pinch} and make a well in the centre. Drop in the @egg yolks{2} and the @oil{1%tbsp}. Mix to a smooth batter with the @milk{150%ml} and beat well. Cover and stand in a cool place for ~{30%minutes}.

Meanwhile, slice the @Spanish onions{2%large} into rings about 1cm wide. Heat the #deep fat fryer{} to 190°C. Whisk the @egg white{1} until stiff and fold into the batter. Then dip the onion rings into the batter in batches and fry until golden brown; this should take 3 to ~{4%minutes}. Serve immediately.